WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.358
Two identical GPUs simplify driver features, memory balance, expected speed, replacement,

00:00:04.358 --> 00:00:05.519
and split planning.

00:00:05.519 --> 00:00:09.390
They do not eliminate communication overhead, slot, lane, power, cooling,

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:10.552
or runtime requirements.

00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:14.035
Mixed NVIDIA GPUs may be practical when reusing hardware,

00:00:14.035 --> 00:00:17.906
but different memory sizes and compute capabilities complicate balanced splits.

00:00:17.906 --> 00:00:21.390
The faster card may wait for the slower one,

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.100
while the smaller card limits some strategies.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:30.294
A GPU plus CPU fallback can fit a model economically when interactive speed is not critical.

00:00:30.294 --> 00:00:36.487
It should be benchmarked with realistic context because CPU-resident work and memory transfer may dominate generation.

00:00:36.487 --> 00:00:41.132
A workstation tower centralizes storage and management but concentrates heat, noise, power,

00:00:41.132 --> 00:00:41.906
and failure.

00:00:41.906 --> 00:00:46.939
Used datacenter GPUs can offer memory value yet may require specialized cooling, power,

00:00:46.939 --> 00:00:48.874
drivers, brackets, or display arrangements.

00:00:48.874 --> 00:00:53.906
External GPU experiments are useful for learning but add enclosure and interface constraints.

00:00:53.906 --> 00:00:59.326
A production design should not assume an experimental link offers desktop-slot behavior or support.

00:00:59.326 --> 00:01:03.197
Multiple single-GPU servers can isolate models, users, failures, and upgrades.

00:01:03.197 --> 00:01:06.681
Networking and orchestration remain, but each node is simpler.

00:01:06.681 --> 00:01:12.874
Separate machines are often better when the goal is parallel workloads rather than one split model.

00:01:12.874 --> 00:01:17.519
A scheduler should understand model residency, memory headroom, queue length, request type,

00:01:17.519 --> 00:01:18.681
and device health.

00:01:18.681 --> 00:01:24.100
Round-robin routing alone can overload a smaller GPU or repeatedly trigger expensive model swaps.
